    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the primary statement line 'Total revenues and other income' is composed of the three listed sub-items. 2. For total_operating_cost, the mapping follows standard practice for the oil & gas industry. It includes all costs directly tied to operations before financing and tax items. Therefore, 'Other taxes and duties' (which are production, property, and severance taxes) are included as part of 'Production and manufacturing expenses' and 'SG&A' per the supplementary note, and are thus captured within those line items. 'Interest expense' and 'Income tax expense' are excluded as they are non-operating. 3. 'Net income' is mapped to the line attributable to the parent company. 4. The supplementary tables for reserves and future cash flows are not direct components of the income statement and are therefore not mapped to the requested fields.",
